Title: Clean up orphaned git-locked worktrees before each beat run
Created: 2026-05-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-10T11:30Z claude created — identified in 0109 denial catalog (Run 20260507T230223Z)

--- body ---
## Context

Killed beat agents leave git-locked worktrees in `.claude/worktrees/`. Subsequent
beat runs fail when housekeeping tries `git worktree remove` on these locked trees:

  fatal: impossible de supprimer un arbre de travail verrouillé

The agent recovered (via `git worktree unlock` + `git worktree remove --force`) but
this causes unnecessary noise and recovery steps. Seen in Run 20260507T230223Z for
`agent-a0142f6c972c40a8b` in chemin-de-voix.

## Actions

1. Identify where beat.py starts its run (housekeeping phase entry point).
2. Before the housekeeping phase, scan `git worktree list` for worktrees whose
   `HEAD` lock file exists but no live PID matches (i.e., orphaned).
3. For each orphaned locked worktree: `git worktree unlock <path>` then
   `git worktree remove --force <path>`.
4. Log each removal to beat-outcomes.jsonl as `phase: cleanup, outcome: removed-orphan`.

## Test

After a simulated killed-agent worktree (create a worktree, add a lock file
with a dead PID), running `make check` or the beat housekeeping phase should
automatically remove it without agent intervention.

## Exit criteria

- Beat housekeeping no longer produces `fatal: impossible de supprimer un arbre
  de travail verrouillé` errors.
- Orphaned worktrees are auto-cleaned at beat start rather than requiring manual
  recovery.
